{
  "slug": "matsuri",
  "family": "tracks",
  "label": "Festival Ground",
  "note": "original — written in the idiom of Fujii Kaze's 「まつり」(2022), not transcribed from it. D major with a yo-scale (D E F# A B) melody over gospel 7ths, 90 BPM (rowLen 3675, rows are 32nds so one pattern is one bar), 12 bars, loops at exactly 32 s. Call Dmaj7 Bm7 Gmaj7 A7, rise Em7 F#m7 Gmaj7 A7, hook Gmaj7 A7 Dmaj7 Bm7 with A7 on beat 3 of bar 12 handing back to bar 1. 7 ch: fue_lead = the hook (the shinobue calls in D5-B5, the hook drops off D6 and answers the opening line inverted), piano_chunk = gospel comp on the & and the \"a\", off the lead's downbeats, organ_pad = one held 3rd/7th a bar, voice-led inside oct 3, soul_bass = root-octave-fifth with a chromatic approach into each bar, base_tom = the taiko (don / doko-don, a full bar of fills every fourth bar), snare_3 = the clap on the backbeat, pipe_hit = the chanchiki on the offbeat eighths.",
